{"title":"Career Roadmap · Statistician","role":"Statistician","summary":"A Statistician designs studies, collects and analyzes data, develops statistical models, interprets uncertainty, and communicates evidence for decision-making.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Mathematics"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Statistician designs studies, collects and analyzes data, develops statistical models, interprets uncertainty, and communicates evidence for decision-making."},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Sc Mathematics graduate, the strongest route is to build substantial capability in statistics, probability, programming and data analysis. For advanced statistician, biostatistician, government statistical-service, research and specialized industry positions, an M.Sc/M.Stat in Statistics or a closely related quantitative field is often highly beneficial and may be required for particular roles."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical work includes:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Designing surveys and experiments"},{"text":"Collecting and cleaning datasets"},{"text":"Probability and statistical analysis"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"},{"text":"Regression and statistical modelling"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Time-series analysis"},{"text":"Statistical inference"},{"text":"Data visualization"},{"text":"Forecasting"},{"text":"Reporting and communicating results"},{"text":"Supporting business, scientific or policy decisions"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Career Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Mathematics + probability fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Statistics + programming"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Statistical modelling + projects"}],[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Statistical Analyst / Junior Analyst"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Statistician / Data Analyst"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior Statistician / Statistical Consultant"}],[{"text":"8+ years"},{"text":"Principal Statistician / Quantitative Lead / Research Specialist"}]]},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Mathematics","Probability + Statistics","R / Python + SQL","Statistical Projects","Junior Statistical / Data Role","Statistician","Senior Statistician","Statistical Consultant / Quantitative Lead"]}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Mathematical & Statistical Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build strong fundamentals rather than immediately jumping into machine learning."},{"type":"h","text":"Mathematics"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Calculus"},{"text":"Linear algebra"},{"text":"Coordinate geometry"},{"text":"Differential equations"},{"text":"Mathematical reasoning"},{"text":"Sequences and series"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Probability"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sample spaces"},{"text":"Events"},{"text":"Conditional probability"},{"text":"Bayes' theorem"},{"text":"Random variables"},{"text":"Probability distributions"},{"text":"Expectation"},{"text":"Variance"},{"text":"Covariance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Introductory statistics"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mean"},{"text":"Median"},{"text":"Mode"},{"text":"Variance"},{"text":"Standard deviation"},{"text":"Percentiles"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Basic data visualization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Statistical Analysis & Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"This should be the transition from pure mathematics to applied quantitative work."},{"type":"h","text":"Statistical methods"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Probability distributions"},{"text":"Sampling distributions"},{"text":"Central Limit Theorem"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"},{"text":"z-test"},{"text":"t-test"},{"text":"Chi-square test"},{"text":"ANOVA"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Simple linear regression"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Programming"},{"type":"h","text":"Python"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python fundamentals"},{"text":"NumPy"},{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"matplotlib"},{"text":"SciPy"},{"text":"statsmodels"}]},{"type":"h","text":"R"},{"type":"p","text":"R is particularly valuable for statistical work."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"R syntax"},{"text":"Data frames"},{"text":"Statistical functions"},{"text":"ggplot2"},{"text":"dplyr"},{"text":"Statistical modelling"},{"text":"R Markdown / Quarto"}]},{"type":"h","text":"SQL"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SELECT"},{"text":"WHERE"},{"text":"GROUP BY"},{"text":"JOIN"},{"text":"Subqueries"},{"text":"CTEs"},{"text":"Window functions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Advanced Statistics & Professional Application"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop deeper statistical capability."},{"type":"h","text":"Regression"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Multiple linear regression"},{"text":"Logistic regression"},{"text":"Polynomial regression"},{"text":"Regularization"},{"text":"Model diagnostics"},{"text":"Multicollinearity"},{"text":"Residual analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Experimental design"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Control groups"},{"text":"Randomization"},{"text":"Blocking"},{"text":"Factorial designs"},{"text":"Sample-size considerations"},{"text":"A/B testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced topics"},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on interests:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Time-series analysis"},{"text":"Survival analysis"},{"text":"Multivariate statistics"},{"text":"Non-parametric statistics"},{"text":"Bayesian statistics"},{"text":"Design of experiments"},{"text":"Survey sampling"},{"text":"Categorical data analysis"}]}]},{"heading":"Core Statistical Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"