ts"},{"text":"Explain results to non-statisticians"},{"text":"Defend methodological choices"},{"text":"Understand data limitations"},{"text":"Communicate uncertainty clearly"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"Build at least 4–6 substantial projects, ideally covering:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hypothesis testing"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"A/B testing"},{"text":"Time-series analysis"},{"text":"Survey/sample analysis"},{"text":"Domain-specific statistical study"}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A student with B.Sc Mathematics should avoid positioning themselves as only a generic \"data analyst.\""},{"type":"p","text":"A stronger profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Mathematics","Statistics","Statistical Programming","Experimental/Quantitative Reasoning"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest long-term progression is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Mathematics","Probability + Statistics","R + Python + SQL","Statistical Projects","Internship","Junior Statistical / Data Role","M.Sc / M.Stat Statistics","Statistician","Senior Statistician","Statistical Scientist / Consultant"]},{"type":"note","label":"Core positioning","text":"Statistician with strong mathematical foundations, statistical inference, programming and domain expertise. For advanced professional and research-level statistician roles, M.Sc/M.Stat in Statistics or a closely related quantitative discipline is the strongest progression after B.Sc Mathematics."}]}]}